# check: fail error[E31b]: x[i] gives a copy of the element, which this call would write while it can reach the collection another way
# E31b (review 6b F1): a method called through x[i] that calls C is not made on the element in place where the program
# has an export fn - C may call it before it returns (X13), and one that grows the collection left the element's
# reference naming the buffer the growth retired: the write was lost. (Here C is usleep, which calls nothing back: the
# rule is by what may happen, as a call through a function value's is)
import "std/io"
import unistd "unistd.h"
type blk struct(n I64) { n }
G mut Vec<blk>
export fn olang_grow(n I64) {
    for i in range n { G.Push(blk(i)) }
}
fn (b mut blk&) Bump() {
    unistd.usleep(0)
    b.n = 99
}
fn main() {
    G.Push(blk(1))
    G[0].Bump()
    io.Println("G[0].n = " $G[0].n " len " $G.Len())!
}
